      "command": "get_backlinks",
      "comment": "The three surviving sources in `bl.source_id ASC` order: B3, B4, B7. Two different ways to serve a fourth row are refused here, and the two are independent: B5 linked and its edge was DROPPED when the later edit removed the token, so a mock reading a stale edge set serves it; B8 still HOLDS its edge (soft-deleting a block does not reindex `block_links`) and is excluded only by the `b.deleted_at IS NULL` join filter — #4848, the state that used to be unrepresentable here. B8 sorts after B7, so a missing join filter appends it rather than reordering. Every token carries `page_id` — the key the backlink UI groups by — so a source served under the wrong owning page fails too: B3/B4 belong to page B2, B7 to page B6.",
      "name": "backlinks_all_in_source_id_order"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "blockId": "S1",
        "limit": 2,
        "scope": {
          "kind": "active",
          "space_id": "$SPACE"
        }
      },
      "command": "get_backlinks",
      "comment": "First page of the same listing: `limit` is honoured, `has_more` is true, and the minted cursor is the `{id}` keyset `Cursor::for_id` builds.",
      "name": "backlinks_page_1"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "blockId": "S1",
        "limit": 2,
        "scope": {
          "kind": "active",
          "space_id": "$SPACE"
        }
      },
      "command": "get_backlinks",
      "comment": "Resumes on `bl.source_id > <cursor id>`: the one remaining source, no overlap, no skip, and the listing ends here.",
      "cursor_from": "backlinks_page_1",
      "name": "backlinks_page_2"
    },
    {
      "args": {
